e  but it's actually the names we never see  that are more interesting there is no  mention of miss casey or mark's wife  gemma scout and i'll get to why that may  be in a bit it's completely possible  that irving has or was working with  former lumen employee pedi and or ragabe  in episode 3 pity tells mark that  someone helped him escape and that there  are people out there wanting to expose a  lumen this could be ragabe irving or  both petey even says to mark that at  lumen i'm your best friend  you're my very good friend this is such  a weird thing to say it's almost as if  petey is implying he has a best friend  on the inside that isn't mark and that  person could be irving along with the  employee list is a map of kier  pennsylvania with a number of locations  of kear employees or at least that's  what's implied considering bert goodman  the man irving fell in love with on the  inside is on that map now it may be  coincidence but all the names on the map  are men irving will later drive to  bert's but has his heart crushed to see  him with another man and it's going to  be super awkward when bert opens the  door to find irving who is banging on it  transformed back into his regular audi  self in season 2 expect us to find out  more about irving's investigation at the  end of episode 7 we learn that miss  casey the wellness counselor is mark  scout's wife gemma it's only when he's  transported to the audi world that he  finds this out and that she's still  alive the whole reason mark chose to  have his life severed was to escape the  pain of dealing with his wife's death  the first scene we see of mark is him  grieving her in his car using a tissue  to wipe away his tears a tissue he'll  find in his innies pocket and throw away  like nothing into a nearby waste  receptacle a metaphor for him throwing  away his grief but as his sister tells  him this is only a band-aid solution for  something much larger forgetting about  her for eight hours a day isn't the same