t  years working her way up in lumen  undercover gathering info and now it was  all going to be for nothing by stopping  hallie and calling milcek to interrupt  dylan kobel is maneuvering her way back  into lumen i mean they have to bring her  back as a reward for single-handedly  stopping what could have been one of the  most disastrous events in lumen history  this would also put her in a position  next season to control the innies and  work alongside them to bring lumen down  one of the weirdest moments in the  finale was when mark and patton  discovered devin's baby and patton  hustles past mark exclaiming to everyone  that he was the one to find the baby  first like who says that who even cares  so long as the baby is found there is  something almost childlike about all of  rickon's friends we have rebecc who has  a bird who pecks at her head patton who  can't even recall why historians before  world war ii didn't call the great war  world war one because world war ii  hadn't  happened yet of course that's absolutely  duh and everyone seems infatuated with  rickon's obviously terrible book but  when audi mark meets rickon it's like  he's meeting his hero that's because his  book the uur has become a sort of  anti-lumen handbook for him remember it  has lines like  your job needs you what if rickon's  friends are all severed people who have  been reintroduced back into the public  with wiped memories hence why they don't  have a lot of basic knowledge and have  warped opinions that have been shaped by  their lives at lumen patton saying he  found the baby first is like him wanting  to be rewarded for doing a good job just  like workers at lumen are rewarded with  egg and melon parties for their good  work this would also explain why they're  also taken in by ricken's book because  it's giving them alternate opinions  about the world other than the ones  they've been indoctrinated with so is  everyone shipped i don't think so  however i think a lot more of them are  than we're led to believe there are two  other things i want to mention before we  end the first is when james egan says  the words the revolving james egan tells  helena that he looks forward to her  being alongside him during this event we  don't really know what this is but it  seems to be some sort of ceremony if i  were to hazard a guess it's when a new  successor takes control of the company  perhaps at the old successor's death and  the old one becomes remembered as a wax  mannequin in the hall of perpetuity jane  would pass on the ceo title to helena  and the process becomes like a revolving  door with one egan family member  replacing another the second thing i  want to discuss which has huge  implications for season two is mark  telling devon about lumen this is our  first non-lumen non-severed individual  who now knows about the dangers of this  program she's also just found out that  her sister-in-law the person who helped  make her brother quote-unquote wonderful  is still alive expect her to join forces  with some of our other characters to  take lumen on i had an absolute blast  watching this first season i will be  coming out with more severance videos so  be sure to like subscribe and leave a  comment on your thoughts and theories  about the show below thanks for watching  everyone for more bad takes you can  catch me on twitter and instagram at  thinkstoryyt and until next time  remember  let's burn this place to the ground  you

